# Intent: Swipe pages, part 4: the wiring. CONFIG_MAIPAI_PAGES (default y) turns the pages on: an indev hook sees every finger (the face, a page or the sheet) and feeds the gesture state machine; the old swipes (left and right volume, up quick settings, down stop) are replaced by it, the edge swipes keep the volume and the stop swipe stays; the avatar's tap-to-listen and the eye, mouth and forehead toggles ignore a touch that was a swipe and every touch while a page or the sheet is up. The wake word (listen wake and the listening status), speech (the speaking status) and a touch on the head (hal_head_touch, press and swipes) bring the face back; a ringing timer does too, and so does a game started by voice or the host (it plays on the top layer and needs the touches). A press that only woke a dimmed screen is read without taking the flag (maipai_screen_peek_wake_touch) so the face still knows it. Overlays pause under a page like under the clock face. The sheet's buttons use the existing code: mute and quiet through the face toggles (the privacy state), the listening light through a new maipai_pref_set, find through a find chirp helper (maipai_sounds_find_chirp, run on the main task), games and timers through their own APIs, More opens the old quick settings panel (Wi-Fi networks, reset, version). Quick actions: find, beep, dance and hello run on the main task. The Pictures page decodes the picture face pack's frames on a task of its own (maipai_picface_frame_*), into a 150 KB PSRAM buffer that exists only while that page shows. Tools: self.pages.status (also the probe), self.pages.get, self.pages.set (saved in flash under pages_cfg in the preferences namespace), self.page.show (a page name, sheet or face) and self.page.tiles (up to six tiles, saved at most every ten minutes under page_tiles). Bench builds also get self.page.bench_swipe and self.page.bench_tap, a finger made of numbers that goes through the same touch point the real panel fills (screen wake rule, LVGL input, gesture machine, pages), so the gestures can be checked with no hand. The panel's own driver writes "no finger" over a hand-made point every few milliseconds, so hal_bridge gets bench-only touch_inject, which makes set_touch_point ignore the driver while a bench finger is down (found in the first bench window: without it most synthetic swipes were lifted at once). Resident internal RAM measured on the bench build: about 510 bytes of state, no timer, no objects.
# Placement: unit (touch behavior and the pages work with no host; the tools are for the settings page and Home)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc and .h (m5stack/StackChan, MIT; patch C03 gave the old swipes), and ours: maipai_picface, maipai_face, maipai_fx, maipai_sounds, maipai_screen, hal_bridge, maipai_listen, hal_head_touch, hal_mcp.cpp, Kconfig.projbuild, sdkconfig.core.defaults.
# Check after a flash (bench image first): self.pages.status answers version 1; swipe left from the face shows the games page and right shows the clock; swipe up from the bottom band opens the sheet and it closes after 6 s; a swipe that starts at the very side edge changes the volume; the wake word returns to the face; a touch on the head returns to the face; self.page.show name=tiles after self.page.tiles shows the dashboard; drag a volume slider on the sheet and the volume changes; the stop swipe still ends a game. List of on-unit checks: docs/design/pages-2026-11-17.md.

